    <note type="Try It" number="7.162">
      <p>A rectangular patio has an area of 180 square feet. The width of the patio is three feet less than the length. Find the length and width of the patio.</p>
    </note>
    <p>In an earlier chapter, we used the Pythagorean Theorem $$\left( a^{2} + b^{2} = c^{2} \right)$$. It gave the relation between the legs and the hypotenuse of a right triangle.</p>
    <p>We will use this formula in the next example.</p>
    <example number="7.82">
      <problem>
        <p>Justine wants to put a deck in the corner of her backyard in the shape of a right triangle, as shown below. The hypotenuse will be 17 feet long. The length of one side will be 7 feet less than the length of the other side. Find the lengths of the sides of the deck.</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>Step 1. Read the problem.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Step 2. Identify what you are looking for.</cell>
              <cell>We are looking for the lengths of the sidesof the deck.</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Step 3. Name what you are looking for.One side is 7 less than the other.</cell>
              <cell>Let x = length of a side of the deckx − 7 = length of other side</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Step 4. Translate into an equation.Since this is a right triangle we can use thePythagorean Theorem.</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{95mu} a^{2} + b^{2} = c^{2}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Substitute in the variables.</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{55mu} x^{2} + {(x - 7)}^{2} = 17^{2}$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Step 5. Solve the equation.</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{11mu} x^{2} + x^{2} - 14x + 49 = 289$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{39mu} 2x^{2} - 14x + 49 = 289$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>It is a quadratic equation, so get zero on one side.</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{31mu} 2x^{2} - 14x - 240 = 0$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the greatest common factor.</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{27mu} 2(x^{2} - 7x - 120) = 0$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the trinomial.</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{32mu} 2(x - 15)(x + 8) = 0$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Use the Zero Product Property.</cell>
              <cell>$$2 \neq 0$$</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{29mu} x - 15 = 0$$</cell>
              <cell>$$x + 8 = 0$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Solve.</cell>
              <cell>$$2 \neq 0$$</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{68mu} x = 15$$</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{31mu} x = -8$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Since x is a side of the triangle, $$x = \text{−8}$$ does notmake sense.</cell>
              <cell>$$2 \neq 0$$</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{68mu} x = 15$$</cell>
              <cell>$$\mspace{31mu}{x = -8}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Find the length of the other side.</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>If the length of one side is</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>then the length of the other side is</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>8 is the length of the other side.</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Step 6. Check the answer.Do these numbers make sense?</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Step 7. Answer the question.</cell>
              <cell>The sides of the deck are 8, 15, and 17 feet.</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
